{
  "name": "gap-processing",
  "version": 3,
  "vars_schema": {
    "project_dir": { "kind": "string", "required": true },
    "cluster_result": { "kind": "object" },
    "verdicts": { "kind": "array" },
    "sieve": { "kind": "object" },
    "_structured_exit": { "kind": "object" }
  },
  "actors": {
    "orchestrator": {
      "kind": "executor",
      "brofile": "gap-processing",
      "durable": true,
      "compaction_anchor": true
    }
  },
  "start": "Cluster",
  "nodes": {
    "Cluster": {
      "actor": "orchestrator",
      "prompt": "You are the CLUSTER node of the gap-processing workflow. Project: ${vars.project_dir}.\n\nGround first per the agentic opening sequence, then pull the active substrate gap queue with bbox_gaps(include_addressed=false, project=\"transcript-search\", json=true) and group the gaps by SEMANTIC THEME — cluster gaps that would be investigated against the same code / commits / subsystem (use code-nav and the graph to judge, not gap_kind). A cluster of one is fine.\n\nReturn strict JSON only, no markdown fences, first byte { and last byte }:\n{\"clusters\":[{\"theme\":\"<short label>\",\"gaps\":[<full gap records: id, gap_kind, domain, dedupe_key, wanted_capability, impact, blocking_level, created_at, evidence>]}]}",
      "on_exit": [
        {
          "op": "parse_json",
          "args": { "from": "${Cluster.output}", "repair_missing_closing_delimiters": true },
          "into_var": "cluster_result",
          "on_failure": "halt"
        }
      ],
      "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "Validate" }
    },
    "Validate": {
      "actor": "",
      "foreach": {
        "items": "${vars.cluster_result.clusters}",
        "as_var": "cluster",
        "index_as": "cluster_index",
        "key": "cluster-${vars.cluster_index}",
        "imports": ["project_dir"],
        "exports": ["atom_result"],
        "parallelism": 4,
        "on_item_failure": "collect_then_halt",
        "collect": { "into_var": "verdicts" },
        "subworkflow": {
          "name": "gap-processing-validate-child",
          "version": 1,
          "vars_schema": {
            "project_dir": { "kind": "string", "required": true },
            "cluster": { "kind": "object", "required": true },
            "atom_handle": { "kind": "object" },
            "atom_wait": { "kind": "object" },
            "atom_status": { "kind": "object" },
            "atom_result": { "kind": "object" }
          },
          "actors": {},
          "start": "InvokeAtom",
          "nodes": {
            "InvokeAtom": {
              "actor": "",
              "on_enter": [
                {
                  "op": "mcp_call",
                  "args": {
                    "server": "blackbox",
                    "tool": "atom_invoke",
                    "arguments": {
                      "atom": "atom:gap-cluster-validator@v1",
                      "args": {
                        "project_dir": "${vars.project_dir}",
                        "cluster_theme": "${vars.cluster.theme}",
                        "gaps": "${vars.cluster.gaps}"
                      },
                      "project_dir": "${vars.project_dir}",
                      "owner": "workflow:${meta.arc_id}"
                    },
                    "timeout_secs": 120
                  },
                  "into_var": "atom_handle",
                  "on_failure": "halt"
                }
              ],
              "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "WaitAtom" }
            },
            "WaitAtom": {
              "actor": "",
              "on_enter": [
                {
                  "op": "mcp_call",
                  "args": {
                    "server": "blackbox",
                    "tool": "bro_wait",
                    "arguments": { "task_id": "${vars.atom_handle.task_id}", "timeout_seconds": 900 },
                    "timeout_secs": 920
                  },
                  "into_var": "atom_wait",
                  "on_failure": "halt"
                },
                {
                  "op": "mcp_call",
                  "args": {
                    "server": "blackbox",
                    "tool": "atom_status",
                    "arguments": { "invocation_id": "${vars.atom_handle.invocation_id}", "owner": "workflow:${meta.arc_id}" },
                    "timeout_secs": 30
                  },
                  "into_var": "atom_status",
                  "on_failure": "halt"
                },
                {
                  "op": "set_var",
                  "args": {
                    "key": "atom_result",
                    "value": {
                      "provenance": {
                        "validator_task_id": "${vars.atom_handle.task_id}",
                        "validator_invocation_id": "${vars.atom_handle.invocation_id}"
                      },
                      "cluster_theme": "${vars.cluster.theme}",
                      "output": "${vars.atom_wait.result}"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "next": { "type": "terminal" }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "next": { "type": "goto", "to": "Sieve" }
    },
    "Sieve": {
      "actor": "orchestrator",
      "prompt": "You are the SIEVE node. Project: ${vars.project_dir}.\n\nThe per-cluster validator results are collected here — one entry per cluster, each shaped {\"provenance\":{\"validator_task_id\":...,\"validator_invocation_id\":...},\"cluster_theme\":...,\"output\":\"<JSON string the validator atom returned: {status, cluster_theme, verdicts:[...]}>\"}:\n${vars.verdicts}\n\nFor EACH collected entry: JSON-parse its \"output\" string to get that cluster's verdict list, and stamp EVERY one of those verdicts with that same entry's \"provenance\" object (the workflow-captured runtime handle — this is the reliable provenance; do not invent ids).\n\nThen merge all verdicts across clusters, GROUP BY class in order landed → dupe → externality → stale → actionable, and SORT BY criticality descending (critical > high > medium > low) within each group.\n\nReturn strict JSON only, no markdown fences, first byte { and last byte }:\n{\"sieve\":{\"landed\":[...],\"dupe\":[...],\"externality\":[...],\"stale\":[...],\"actionable\":[...]}}\nEach verdict keeps its fields plus the stamped \"provenance\".",
      "on_exit": [
        {
          "op": "parse_json",
          "args": { "from": "${Sieve.output}", "repair_missing_closing_delimiters": true },
          "into_var": "sieve",
          "on_failure": "halt"
        },
        {
          "op": "set_var",
          "args": { "key": "_structured_exit", "value": "${vars.sieve}" }
        }
      ],
      "next": { "type": "terminal" }
    }
  }
}
